{
  "reviews": [
    {
      "actor": "ash-2",
      "decision": "reuse",
      "ability": "bark-extraction",
      "reason": "The implemented bark-extraction capability already provides the requested functional effect: assessing woody material and separating usable bark from a finite branch outer layer with conserved mass and paid work. It requires an actual inspected stone or flint contact; your current empty inventory does not satisfy that requirement. The reported branch source must be validated against actual observed state. No bark stock, tools, standing-tree tissue or extraction success is assumed.",
      "specification": "Reuse the existing bark-extraction contract unchanged; individual study takes two rounds and is separate from implementation and actual use. Its assess operation costs one round and 0.2 energy. Peeling requires actual eligible branch material and a personally inspected reusable stone or flint contact, costing two active work-round equivalents and two energy per original branch unit, proportionally reduced for fractional or previously peeled material. An unspecified intact branch contributes at most 10% of its existing mass as outer layer; exact-tenth bark units round down, with remaining separated mass retained as bark-fines. Only actual output satisfying the root-preparation bark requirement is usable there; fines and peeled cores are not interchangeable aliases for intact inputs. Use the existing shared reference parameters, ownership checks, interaction geometry, progress and completion schema. Maintain actual remaining work and material provenance; cancellation, including death, must preserve accounted partial material and escrow ownership without duplication or deletion. Standing trunks lacking represented extractable tissue remain ineligible. No new interface, physical mechanism or resource is needed.",
      "experienceReview": "Use the existing practice:bark-extraction source rather than create an alias reward. Subscribe to practice-confirmed from bark-extraction only when qualified under its implemented paid, completed-practice rule with real changed outputs and limited milestones. The performing actor receives amount 0.4, cap 0.5, duration 8, refresh repetition and cooldown 12; maintained satisfaction gains 0.02 on qualifying events and decays 0.001 without them. This recognizes grounded practical progress, not acquisition of a label or mastery. Requesting, assessment alone, learning and merely owning bark earn nothing. No additional transient pleasure is established by peeling itself, and extraction does not directly improve health, hunger, fatigue or temperature.",
      "visualReview": "Reuse bark-assessed, bark-peeling-started, bark-peeling-progress, bark-peeling-completed and bark-peeling-stopped for presentation subscriptions, with practice-confirmed bound separately to experience feedback. Show the actual selected branch and contact tool, paid progress and remaining work, finite outer-layer removal, retained core, bark and fines with their represented quantities. Cancellation must display the actual partial result rather than a completed product. Use existing material locations and shared interaction geometry; do not display invented standing-tree damage, tools or bark stock.",
      "learning": 2
    }
  ]
}

